=== HINT 1: Writer - create + map ===
HANDLE hmap = CreateFileMapping(INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE, NULL, PAGE_READWRITE,
                                 0, SHM_SIZE, SHM_NAME);
ShmBlock *blk = (ShmBlock *)MapViewOfFile(hmap, FILE_MAP_WRITE, 0, 0, SHM_SIZE);
strcpy(blk->message, "Hello from writer!");
InterlockedExchange(&blk->magic, MAGIC);   // publish atomically

=== HINT 2: Reader - open + map ===
HANDLE hmap = OpenFileMapping(FILE_MAP_READ, FALSE, SHM_NAME);
const ShmBlock *blk = (const ShmBlock *)MapViewOfFile(hmap, FILE_MAP_READ, 0, 0, SHM_SIZE);

=== HINT 3: Spin-wait ===
while (InterlockedCompareExchange((volatile LONG*)&blk->magic, MAGIC, MAGIC) != MAGIC)
    Sleep(1);
printf("Reader got: %s\n", blk->message);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Writer uses PAGE_READWRITE / FILE_MAP_WRITE.
Reader uses PAGE_READONLY / FILE_MAP_READ.
Both name "CFarerShm" - the kernel routes them to the same physical pages.
InterlockedExchange ensures the magic write is not reordered before the message.
